{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"peacocky-playful-echidna","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Why\nAGENTS.md is the canonical, cross-vendor agent guidance. CLAUDE.md bridges Claude Code to it\nvia an @AGENTS.md import, and .codex/config.toml points Codex's project_doc_fallback at it.\nGitHub Copilot's coding agent already reads AGENTS.md natively, but other Copilot surfaces\n(Copilot Chat, Copilot CLI) look at .github/copilot-instructions.md first and had no pointer\nback to AGENTS.md, so they could silently drift from the canonical guidance.\n\n## What\nAdd .github/copilot-instructions.md as a thin bridge file (mirroring CLAUDE.md's role): it\ndeclares AGENTS.md authoritative, summarizes the key sections (ticket workflow, Gerrit git\nflow, module-size policy, code-navigation tooling), and explicitly says not to duplicate\ncontent that could drift.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- .github/copilot-instructions.md exists, references AGENTS.md as canonical/authoritative,\n  and does not restate AGENTS.md content beyond a short summary.\n- No local-only Copilot state is added to the tracked tree (mirrors the posture where\n  CLAUDE.local.md and .codex/worktrees stay untracked/local-only).\n- Change lands through Gerrit per CONTRIBUTING.md (rebar-ticket trailer, DCO sign-off,\n  LLM-Review +1, Verified +1).","id":"f1db-f250-e38b-4ffe","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Add .github/copilot-instructions.md bridge file for provider-guidance parity"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785544433238089001,"uuid":"deff68df-c9ca-47c2-9310-5419acea223e"}